---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle="about">
  <h1>I'm Jamie</h1>
  <section>
    <p>I've been coding on the web since 2009.</p>
    <p>
      I've worked in engineeriing positions at agencies and product companies in
      sectors including automotive, ecommerce and recruitment. Currently I'm
      employed as a Senior Frontend Engineer at <a
        href="https://www.beamery.com">Beamery</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      This is my small section of the internet where I share my learnings.
      Before we start, I should warn you that I'm not much of a writer or an
      expert in anything really - I'm just a developer who enjoys the web and
      likes to learn about it and if I'm being totally honest I'm writing this
      more as a reminder for myself. Consider the posts here a slimmed down,
      learn the basics type of thing. If you are after a comprehensive guide on
      a topic I reccommend the articles on <a href="https://css-tricks.com/"
        >CSS-Tricks</a
      > or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/">MDN Web Docs</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
